This directory is the root of the Visual Studio Code extension that knows how
to set breakpoints in a .cbl file.  With breakpoints set, you can use Visual
Studio Code to launch the cobst/obmod modified executable.

As of this writing, the variables window will show the variables from the
intermediate .C file generated as part of the cobc/gcc/gas/ld process.  But the
DEBUGGER OUTPUT window can be used to "p COBOL-VARIABLE".

Bob Dubner, 2019-08-14
